'''Gauntlets''' (強襲ステージ, ''Kyōshū Sutēji'', '''Assault Stages''') are a type of event introduced in the [[Version 9.3 Update]].

==Overview==
A Gauntlet is a map containing up to 20 [[No Continues]] stages  that can drop rewards such as [[Battle Items]], [[Catfruit]], [[Cat Capsule|Tickets]], [[Gamatoto Expedition|Catamins]], [[Ototo Corps|Materials]] and [[Leadership]]s when completed for the first time. Players can score up to three victories within the Gauntlet before it becomes inaccessible, and each takes 30 minutes or 1 [[Catamin]] A to refill.

In most Gauntlets, all stages play out the same, but the strength magnifications and enemy base's HP are increased with each stage. Gauntlets also tend to have enemies with separate health and attack magnifications instead of a universal multiplier as a balance.

Similar to [[Heavenly Tower]], [[Infernal Tower]] and [[Legend Quest]], all progress made in a Gauntlet will reset when the event ends, allowing the player to collect the rewards again once the event returns. As of [[Version 12.5 Update|Version 12.5]], Gauntlets also have a checkpoint system that allows the player to start from stage 10 once the player has cleared stage 10, like in the towers and Legend Quest.

==Colossus Gauntlets==
The Colossus Gauntlets don't follow any specific schedule, and can only be played after clearing [[Into the Future]] Chapter 3. Each contains a unique boss with two types: a regular trait and [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]], a special type that makes them weak to [[:Category:Colossus Slayer Cats|Colossus Slayers]]. There are two sets of enemies per Gauntlet, one for Lv.1~10 and another for Lv.11~20.[[File:E 499.png|thumb|[[Baron Seal|Baron Seal]], the first example of a Colossus]]

Beating the stages in these Gauntlets may give you the chance to play one of three Continuation Stages that have a much more consistent drop rate of Strong Effect Up, Tough Effect Up or Massive Damage Up [[Talent Orbs]] for the respective boss's primary trait. The Continuation Stages are always named Cradle Wilderness, Summit Wilderness and Frontier Wilderness, but the level design is different for each Gauntlet.

One of Gauntlets listed below will appear every other week lasting for one week.

