==Trivia==
*The map used in many of the Gauntlets (shown in the gallery above) appears to be based on a map of the Japanese city of Kyoto, especially the river.
*Gauntlets and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 41|Floor 41]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]] are currently the only [[Leadership]]-dropping stages not only found after clearing the whole map.
*There was no official English name for this type of stage until [[Version 10.6 Update|Version 10.6]], which introduced the first Monthly Gauntlets.
*In the English changelog for [[Version 12.5 Update|Version 12.5]], the Gauntlets with their own [[:Category:Colossus Enemies|Colossus]] bosses were officially named "Colossus Gauntlets".
*The [[Manbosaki Strikes! (Old)|original version]] of Manbosaki Strikes! was the only Gauntlet to have 12 stages.
*Prior to [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]], Gauntlets were locked for 30 minutes immediately upon each clear, rather than a total of 90 minutes after three.
*[[Great Angel Chibinel]] is the only enemy in a Colossus [[Gauntlet]] to not get incrementally buffed, appearing at 100% in [[Attack of the Omens/Three Omens Lv.1~20|Three Omens Lv.1~10]].

